      },
      "text": "Solving Ax = b is the most common operation in scientific computing. Every PDE solver, least-squares regression, and iterative optimizer reduces to linear solves. The choice between direct and iterative methods depends on problem size and structure."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  LINEAR SYSTEM SOLVER TAXONOMY                   |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  DIRECT METHODS                    ITERATIVE METHODS             |\n|  (exact up to rounding)            (converge to solution)       |\n|  +---------------------+           +-------------------+        |\n|  | LU factorization    |           | CG (sym. PD)      |        |\n|  | Ax=b, dense         |           | GMRES (general)   |        |\n|  | O(n^3) work         |           | BiCGSTAB          |        |\n|  | O(n^2) storage      |           | MINRES (sym.)     |        |\n|  +---------------------+           | Multigrid         |        |\n|  | QR factorization    |           +-------------------+        |\n|  | Least squares min   |           | O(n) to O(n^4/3)  |        |\n|  | ||Ax-b||^2          |           | for sparse A      |        |\n|  +---------------------+           +-------------------+        |\n|  | Cholesky (sym.PD)   |           PRECONDITIONING:             |\n|  | A = LL^T            |           Key to practical speed       |\n|  | Half the work of LU |                                        |\n|  -----------------------                                        |\n|  WHEN DIRECT:          n < 10^4, dense, need exact solution     |\n|  WHEN ITERATIVE:       n > 10^4, sparse, structured             |\n|                                                                 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
