      "text": "## Gaussian Elimination and LU Factorization"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Gaussian elimination** transforms Ax = b into Ux = c (upper triangular) by row operations:"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  FORWARD ELIMINATION:\n  For k = 1 to n-1:\n    For i = k+1 to n:\n      m_ik = A_{ik} / A_{kk}   (multiplier; A_{kk} = pivot)\n      For j = k to n:\n        A_{ij} = A_{ij} - m_ik * A_{kj}\n      b_i = b_i - m_ik * b_k"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BACK SUBSTITUTION:\n  x_n = b_n / A_{nn}\n  x_i = (b_i - Sum_{j=i+1}^n A_{ij} x_j) / A_{ii}   for i = n-1 down to 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COST: O(n^3) flops (2n^3/3 for elimination + O(n^2) for back substitution)\n  STORAGE: O(n^2)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**LU factorization** decomposes A = LU (L lower triangular, U upper triangular):"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  L_{ik} = m_ik (multipliers stored below diagonal of \"A\")\n  U_{kj} = A_{kj} after elimination (upper triangular result)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SOLVE Ax = b using A = LU:\n  Ly = b (forward substitution, O(n^2))\n  Ux = y (back substitution, O(n^2))"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ADVANTAGE: Factorize ONCE (O(n^3)), solve MANY times (O(n^2) each).\n  For solving with multiple right-hand sides b_1, b_2, ...: one factorization suffices.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#014",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Partial pivoting** (essential for stability):"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  PROBLEM: If A_{kk} is small, the multipliers m_ik = A_{ik}/A_{kk} are large.\n  Large multipliers amplify rounding errors. UNSTABLE without pivoting."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#016",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PARTIAL PIVOTING: before elimination step k, find row with largest |A_{ik}| for i >= k.\n  Swap that row with row k. Record the permutation."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#017",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "section": "numerical-methods",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Linear Systems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PA = LU factorization with permutation matrix P.\n  Solve Ax = b: Ly = Pb, then Ux = y."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md#018",
      "path": [
        "02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems, git-history:numerical-methods:02-linear-systems]",
        "canonical_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "concepts": "[linear, systems]",
        "current_path": "numerical-methods/02-LINEAR-SYSTEMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:numerical-methods:linear-systems",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "numerical-methods",
